<html xmlns:o="urn:schemas-microsoft-com:office:office" xmlns:w="urn:schemas-microsoft-com:office:word" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/TR/REC-html40">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<title>System Features Description</title>
<style>
    body { font-family: 'Calibri', 'Arial', sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; line-height: 1.4; }
    h1 { color: #2F5496; font-size: 20pt; border-bottom: 2px solid #2F5496; padding-bottom: 5px; }
    table { width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; margin-top: 20px; }
    th { background-color: #2F5496; color: white; padding: 10px; text-align: left; border: 1px solid #1F3864; }
    td { border: 1px solid #d9d9d9; padding: 10px; vertical-align: top; }
    tr:nth-child(even) { background-color: #f2f2f2; }
    b { color: #1F3864; }
</style>
</head>
<body>

    <h1>EuroTaxi System - Features Description</h1>
    <p>A brief description of each feature included in your system.</p>

    <table>
        <tr>
            <th width="35%">Feature Name</th>
            <th width="65%">Short Description</th>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td><b>Driver Support System</b></td>
            <td>Internal messaging platform for direct communication and quick resolution of driver concerns and inquiries.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td><b>Announcement</b></td>
            <td>System for posting and pinning general news and reminders for all employees and drivers to read.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td><b>Notification</b></td>
            <td>Real-time push alerts that inform users about important events (e.g., system updates, SOS alerts, test chimes).</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td><b>History Logs</b></td>
            <td>Complete record or "audit trail" of all actions performed by each user within the system for transparency and security tracking.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td><b>Archive Management</b></td>
            <td>A repository where deleted data (soft deletes) are temporarily stored so they can either be restored or permanently removed (force delete).</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td><b>General Staff Records</b></td>
            <td>Roster and profile management for general employees (office staff, mechanics, etc.) excluding administrators and app drivers.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td><b>Admin Staff</b></td>
            <td>Management of employees granted administrative access and special control over the system configuration.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td><b>Mobile app staff</b></td>
            <td>Roster and credential management for employees or drivers who use the mobile application for their daily work.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td><b>Unit Details</b></td>
            <td>Detailed profile of each taxi or vehicle including the plate number, engine number, and its current status (active or under maintenance).</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td><b>Owner Panel</b></td>
            <td>The highest-level control panel (Super Admin) where core system settings are modified and all account types are managed.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td><b>Page access</b></td>
            <td>Security feature to restrict or grant permissions to each user regarding which specific pages or modules they are allowed to access.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td><b>Log in History</b></td>
            <td>Security log that lists the exact time, date, and IP address of every user's login session.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td><b>Banned Drivers Roster</b></td>
            <td>List of drivers who are suspended or permanently banned from driving for the company due to severe violations or offenses.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td><b>Driver Contract of Rent</b></td>
            <td>Module to upload, manage, and securely record the signed contracts (terms and conditions) between the driver and the operator.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td><b>Financial Liabilities</b></td>
            <td>Section where outstanding balances, pending debts, and payment histories of the drivers are continuously tracked.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td><b>Kill Engine</b></td>
            <td>Remote command feature (via Live Tracking) used to cut off or disable the vehicle's engine securely using the installed GPS device.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td><b>Franchise Decision Management</b></td>
            <td>Management of documents and formal management decisions regarding unit franchises or company legal matters.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td><b>Boundary Management</b></td>
            <td>The core financial system that records daily boundary payments and calculates the net income generated by the drivers.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td><b>Maintenance Management</b></td>
            <td>Module for tracking vehicles under repair, spare parts consumed, and overall maintenance or mechanic expenses.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td><b>Coding Schedule Management</b></td>
            <td>Automated tracking of each vehicle's number coding schedule to prevent traffic violations and fines on the road.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td><b>Driver Performance & Violations</b></td>
            <td>Record of driver behavior, performance ratings, and logs of their traffic violations or reported incidents on the road.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td><b>Weekly Incentives</b></td>
            <td>Bonus issuance system for drivers with perfect daily attendance, zero traffic violations, and complete boundary remittances in a week.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td><b>Performance Summary</b></td>
            <td>A comprehensive summary of a driver's overall record, combining their financial reliability (boundary/debts) and behavioral aspect (violations).</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td><b>Accidents Reports</b></td>
            <td>System for receiving emergency alerts (SOS) and logging traffic accidents for rapid response and documentation.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td><b>Office Expenses</b></td>
            <td>Section where all internal office expenses such as electricity, water, and office supplies are recorded, reviewed, and approved.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td><b>Salary Management</b></td>
            <td>Payroll system that calculates, manages, and records the monthly salaries of all in-house staff and mechanics.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td><b>Advanced Fleet Analytics</b></td>
            <td>In-depth data analysis using interactive graphs to monitor the overall health, performance, and operational status of the entire vehicle fleet.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td><b>Real-Time Pulse</b></td>
            <td>Live dashboard displaying the most recent company status (active units, online drivers, today's total revenue) updated every second.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td><b>Descriptive Analytics</b></td>
            <td>Visual heatmaps and charts explaining 'what happened' in the past based on historical system records and aggregated data.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td><b>Predictive Forecasting</b></td>
            <td>Using historical data patterns and trends to predict future outcomes, such as estimating potential revenues or forecasting maintenance expenses.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td><b>AI Strategic Insights</b></td>
            <td>Intelligent recommendations generated by AI providing data-driven advice or solutions to the operator to further optimize business operations.</td>
        </tr>
    </table>

</body>
</html>
